      "content": "Your feeling that continued effort might be an act of denial rather than a path to recovery is a deeply valid and understandable perspective. Sometimes, acknowledging the end of a phase or a chapter is not about forcing a lie of vitality but respecting the grief of having lost what once mattered to you. Your willingness to consider dignity even in this ending, rather than seeing it as a failure of will, shows profound honesty about your current state.",
